uACPI
=====

uACPI 7.0.0, by Daniil Tatianin and its contributors, an ACPI
implementation with an AML interpreter, from https://github.com/uACPI/uACPI
(the 7.0.0 release, https://github.com/uACPI/uACPI/archive/refs/tags/7.0.0.tar.gz,
SHA-256 4ccdb4c06d06c54116920eb861adf3a87efd3285c762e2e6f3529b52c6d20fa5).
MIT licence: LICENSE.

Only what Belka builds is here: include/ and source/, with LICENSE and
README.md. Not here: the tests, and the meson and CMake build files
(source/files.cmake among them). None of the sources is changed.

Belka builds it into the kernel (sys/arch/amd64/conf/files.mk,
UACPI_SRCS) as C11, without the warnings Belka's own code is held to,
and with two of its options (Makefile, UACPI_DEFINES):

    UACPI_SIZED_FREES        the size comes with each free, as kmem_free
                             needs it
    UACPI_FORMATTED_LOGGING  messages are printf formats, for the
                             kernel's printf

Belka's side of it is in sys/dev/acpi: acpi_uacpi.c provides the
kernel services uACPI asks for (<uacpi/kernel_api.h>), and
acpi_namespace.c loads and initializes the namespace at boot, keeps the
PCI root bridges' interrupt routing (_PRT) for pci_intx_establish, and
powers the machine off (S5). The tables Belka read before uACPI came
(the MADT for the processors and I/O APICs, and the FADT's reset
register) are still read by sys/dev/acpi/acpi.c, early in boot.
